	abstract = {The increasing penetration of renewable energy into modern power systems has introduced significant operational challenges, including uncertainty, nonlinearity, and intermittency. This paper proposes a machine learning-integrated adaptive control and performance optimization framework to address dynamic efficiency and stability issues in renewable energy systems. The framework combines real-time adaptive control theory with predictive intelligence based on reinforcement learning and Gaussian process regression. Using a hybrid approach, it enables self-learning of system behavior under varying operating conditions and dynamically adjusts control parameters to optimize energy conversion efficiency. Simulation and experimental results on a hybrid photovoltaic-wind-battery system demonstrate that the proposed framework significantly enhances stability compared to traditional PID and model predictive control methods. This research establishes a scalable, data-driven control foundation for building resilient and high-performance renewable energy management systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
