	abstract = {Over the last decades, Renewable energy sources are widely applied in distribution networks due to the increased demand for the electrical energy. The improper placement and sizing of renewable energy based {DGs} (distributed generations) may increase the losses in the network and also lead to voltage collapse in severe cases. This paper treats the problem of optimal sitting and sizing of solar photovoltaic {DGs} in distribution network using the evolutionary technique {SPEA}2 (Strength Pareto Evolutionary Algorithm 2). The objective is to minimize the active power loss and the annual operation cost within the framework of system operational and security constraints in distribution systems. The optimization problem is applied on {IEEE} 33 bus distribution network. The obtained results prove the efficiency of the proposed technique in finding the optimal location and sizing of solar {DGs}. © 2016 {IEEE}.},
