	doi = {10.3390/en10050620},
	abstract = {This paper presents an overview of our body of work on the application of smart control techniques for the control and management of microgrids ({MGs}). The main focus here is on the application of distributed multi-agent system ({MAS}) theory in multi-objective ({MO}) power management of {MGs} to find the Pareto-front of the {MO} power management problem. In addition, the paper presents the application of Nash bargaining solution ({NBS}) and the {MAS} theory to directly obtain the {NBS} on the Pareto-front. The paper also discusses the progress reported on the above issues from the literature. We also present a {MG}-based power system architecture for enhancing the resilience and self-healing of the system. © 2017 by the authors.},
