	abstract = {'Electric heating' is an inevitable trend under the goal of 'peak carbon dioxide emissions and carbon neutrality', and the optimization control of solar heat storage microgrid, as an important component of smart grid optimization, it is of great significance to reduce energy consumption and environmental pollution. The goal of microgrid development is not only to meet the basic needs of power supply, but also to improve economic efficiency and protect the environment. In this paper, a microgrid multi-objective optimization control model is proposed, which considers the daily operating cost and carbon emission cost of the microgrid system. At the same time, the improved particle swarm optimization algorithm is used to solve the optimization model. Simulation results show that the model can effectively reduce heating costs and environmental pollution, promote the optimization of microgrid operation, and verify the superior performance of the improved particle swarm optimization algorithm. © 2023 {IEEE}.},
