	isbn = {978-1-6654-9899-9},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85148447022&doi=10.1109%2fCEECT55960.2022.10030661&partnerID=40&md5=3ce3eb8f1e569edd31a98abba6540cf0},
	doi = {10.1109/CEECT55960.2022.10030661},
	abstract = {Aiming at the need of peak-load shifting and the uncertainty of wind and photovoltaic power, this paper proposes a double layer virtual power plant scheduling model that integrates wind, photovoltaic power, gas turbine, power-to-gas device, energy storage devices and cooling heating and power microgrid. A Markov Chain Monte Carlo method is used to deal with the uncertainty of wind and photovoltaic power. In the upper layer {VPP} scheduling, the source side preferentially uses wind and photovoltaic energy, and the load side guides the load distribution through demand response measures such as {TOU} price and flexible load compensation. In the lower level {VPP} scheduling, the {NSGA}-{II} algorithm is utilized to the multi-objective optimization model by taking the minimum {VPP} operation cost and the lowest carbon emission as the objective function. The simulation results show that the proposed {VPP} scheduling model can effectively deal with the uncertainty of renewable energy output, and take into account environmental protection and economy of the system, so as to realize the low-carbon and economic operation of the system.  © 2022 {IEEE}.},
