	isbn = {979-8-3503-3775-4},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85178056594&doi=10.1109%2fSAFEPROCESS58597.2023.10295658&partnerID=40&md5=2b4b47e6619d96d2060bcf36909e9162},
	doi = {10.1109/SAFEPROCESS58597.2023.10295658},
	abstract = {The greenhouse integrated energy system that complements agriculture and fishing has strong uncertainty. The traditional electric heating separation method and the hierarchical scheduling operation mode of the transmission and distribution grid are no longer able to achieve the global optimal operation strategy, reducing the energy ladder utilization rate and economic and environmental benefits.In order to improve the system's absorption of new energy and the ability of multi-energy complementarity, this paper puts forward a dynamic response characteristic of agricultural and fishery complementary greenhouse integrated energy optimization scheduling strategy. Firstly, establish a comprehensive energy system relationship matrix, introduce a carbon trading model into the integrated energy system that complements agriculture and fishing, and improve the level of environmental protection.Secondly, an optimization model for the comprehensive energy system of source load storage was constructed, and a layered operational architecture was proposed to meet the dynamic needs of greenhouses and demand side living. Finally, simulation examples were used to verify the effectiveness of this method. The results showed that it can reduce equipment energy supply pressure and carbon emissions, optimize system operation, and improve system economy and environmental benefits.  © 2023 {IEEE}.},
