	isbn = {978-1-6654-1025-0},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85124013167&doi=10.1109%2fICECEM54757.2021.00096&partnerID=40&md5=46242910a27603c390578fb6a89ab8d1},
	doi = {10.1109/ICECEM54757.2021.00096},
	abstract = {During the operation of the microgrid, the output power of some distributed power sources is fluctuating and intermittent, which will bring huge challenges to the planning and operation of the microgrid. In view of the high penetration rate of renewable energy connected to the microgrid, combined with the effect of the energy storage device in the microgrid on peak shaving and valley filling of the grid according to the changes in user demand at different times and the difference in electricity prices, this paper formulates energy dispatch under dynamic market pricing. The goal is to minimize economic costs and minimize environmental pollution during system operation. By adjusting the switch state of the controllable unit, the charge and discharge state of the energy storage battery, and the interaction between the microgrid and the large grid, when formulate the best control sequence of each unit in every cycle. The improved fast non-dominated sorting genetic algorithm ({NSGA}-{II}) is used to find the Pareto optimal solutions for the four scenarios. Through the analysis of the energy scheduling strategy and the non-adopted scheduling strategy, the results show that the proposed scheduling strategy can effectively reduce the economic cost and optimize the environmental benefits, verifying the effectiveness of the proposed method.  © 2021 {IEEE}.},
