	isbn = {979-8-3503-6469-9},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-86000015355&doi=10.1109%2fIC3TES62412.2024.10877626&partnerID=40&md5=6b143c2e4a29c3e25f7a9f5e75324592},
	doi = {10.1109/IC3TES62412.2024.10877626},
	abstract = {The research area of interest covers the application of mathematical optimization, and control theory in power electronics interfacing renewable energy systems to achieve higher efficiency, reliability and system performance. In this context, the Paper's key strengths are proposed as follows: By identifying the suitable datasets and designing the improved optimization techniques like genetic algorithm, particle swarm optimization, and neural network the proposed methodology intends to overcome the issue associated with the variability and intermittency of the renewable energy sources. Ensured to work with efficient software tools like {MATLAB}/Simulink and Python the methodology has undergone simulation and real world tests. Results demonstrated significant improvements: efficiency was raised to a level of 7-8\%, at the same time as the cost was decreased in the range of 16\%. Between 7-20\%, power quality had received improvement in voltage and frequency fluctuations that was reduced to half; while the reliability factor increased to 5\%. The outcomes of this study underscore the ability of multi-objective optimization in development of proper balanced solutions for the analysis of renewable energy system. Furthermore, the study stresses the necessity of a steady examination and fine-tuning process for the effective incorporation of {RES} into the power grid and the effective and eco-friendly power supply. As for the future works, Component performance optimization, compatibility with current infrastructure and effective control of large distributed generation should be the focus of future researches. © 2024 {IEEE}.},
