	abstract = {Currently, most of China's new energy sources are large-scale wind farms and photovoltaic power generation bases. The grid connection of such In order to ensure the reliability requirements of the power system, inevitable phenomena such as wind and solar curtailment often occur. In order to ensure the reliability requirements of the power system, inevitable phenomena such as wind and solar curtailment often occur, which not only affects the economic efficiency of the power system but also hinders the development of new energy. Studying the output characteristics of new energy, establishing a simulation model for power system operation that is suitable for large-scale new energy integration, and the development of new energy. suitable for large-scale new energy integration, improving the consumption capacity of new energy through optimized configuration of new energy, is conducive to the sustainable development of new energy. conducive to the sustainable development of new energy industry and the reliable and safe economic operation of power system. Therefore, this article will conduct research on reliability evaluation methods for new energy grids that have been added. Firstly, the difference between the new energy grid and the conventional power system lies in the fact that the new energy grids have been added. Firstly, the difference between the new energy grid and the conventional power system lies in the severe impact of weather. Historical meteorological data is used for analysis, and weather type clustering is carried out based on the characteristics of weather type. Historical meteorological data is used for analysis, and weather type clustering is carried out based on the characteristics of wind and solar power output. Secondly, analyze the influencing factors of wind and solar power generation, establish an indicator system to evaluate the complementarity of wind and solar power generation. Secondly, analyze the influencing factors of wind and 