	abstract = {The problem of multitime scale coordinated scheduling for electric vehicles ({EVs}) with vehicle-to-grid (V2G) technology is formulated for a microgrid with photovoltaic/wind/battery generation. The life of the energy storage system in the microgrid, and the benefits for {EV} users are considered as the optimization goals. Reasonable measures of the charging and discharging behaviors of {EVs} are considered to construct the objective functions. A stratified sequencing method is designed to transform the multiobjective optimization problem into a single-objective nonlinear optimization problem that can be solved through adaptive particle swarm optimization ({APSO}). Then an optimal multitime scale coordinated scheduling scheme can be obtained. The effectiveness and feasibility of the methods are verified by simulation results. © 2019 John Wiley \& Sons, Ltd.},
