	doi = {10.1109/IMCEC59810.2024.10575372},
	abstract = {In the realm of smart grids, the optimized scheduling of microgrids occupies a pivotal position, significantly impacting energy consumption and environmental pollution reduction. The development of microgrids must ensure stability and reliability of power supply, while also contributing to economic efficiency and environmental friendliness. To this end, this study presents a multi-objective optimization scheduling model that comprehensively addresses operational and environmental protection costs within grid-connected operational modes. An particle swarm optimization algorithm is introduced for solving this model. Simulation results validate the model's in lowering electricity costs and mitigating environmental pollution.  © 2024 {IEEE}.},
